{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Cursed be he who does not uphold the words of this Torah.</b> This is a general principle for all the commandments in the Torah. The meaning of the verse is: who does not establish the commandments in his heart — that is, that he should acknowledge them and believe in all of them that they are truth, not one of them being absent, and that there is in them benefit for body and soul, and that there is not in all of them a single commandment for naught. This is 'who does not uphold to do them' — that he should establish in his heart a firm faith that it is proper to do them, for all of them are נכוחים למבין וישרים למוצאי דעת (straight to the one who understands, upright to those who find knowledge) (Proverbs 8:9). <br>And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: 'who does not uphold' — one who does not lift up a Torah scroll to show its writing to the people."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:29.650096357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}